/-!
# Louboutin's Conjecture 6.1 in an abstract biquadratic model

Model (`Louboutin.Conj61.V4Data O`): `O` a commutative domain of characteristic `0` (think `𝓞_K`),
four distinct elements `x 0, …, x 3` (the conjugates of `α = x 0`), three ring endomorphisms
`τ₁, τ₂, τ₃` acting on them by the labelling `τ_i x_k = x_{i xor k}`, and `fix`: an element fixed
by `τ₁, τ₂, τ₃` is an integer (for `𝓞_K` with `Gal(K/ℚ) ≅ V₄`, `𝓞_K^G = ℤ`). `Zα` is the
`ℤ`-span of `1, α, α², α³` (`= ℤ[α]`, `Zα_mul_mem`); "`ℤ[α]` Galois-invariant" means that every
conjugate lies in `Zα`.

The route avoids content ideals over `𝓞_K`: for each `j`, `r_j²` and `r_j ΔQ_j` are invariant,
hence integers; dividing by their gcd gives `r_j = n_j ϑ_j`, `ΔQ_j = t_j ϑ_j` with `ϑ_j ∈ O`
(Bézout), `Θ = ϑ₁ϑ₂ϑ₃` is an integer `θ`, and `P(X) = θ ∏(n_j X + t_j)` with a primitive
product (Gauss's lemma, `IsPrimitive.mul`).

## Main results

* `Louboutin.Conj61.V4Data.thm2`: an integer dividing `T, U, V, W` divides every `N_jk`.
* `Louboutin.Conj61.V4Data.gcd_TUVW`: `gcd(T, U, V, W) = |θ|`.
* `Louboutin.Conj61.V4Data.conj61`: Conjecture 6.1, `ℤ[α]` is invariant iff `Δ = Vand` divides
  `T, U, V, W`.
* `Louboutin.Conj61.V4Data.exists_ints`: `T, U, V, W, Δ` are integers, `Δ ≠ 0` and `Δ` is even.
* `Louboutin.Conj61.V4Data.cor_weak`, `Louboutin.Conj61.V4Data.conj61_weak`: invariance iff
  `Δ ∣ T, U, V ± W`.

## References

* S. R. Louboutin, *On the order generated by the conjugates of an algebraic integer*, in:
  Algebra, Logic and Number Theory, Banach Center Publ. 121 (2020), 107–124, doi:10.4064/bc121-10.
* S. R. Louboutin, *When is the order generated by a cubic, quartic or quintic algebraic unit Galois
  invariant: three conjectures*, Czechoslovak Math. J. 70 (2020), 905–919,
  doi:10.21136/CMJ.2020.0019-19.
* C. Marín, *Orders generated by conjugates of Galois quartic integers*, preprint (2026).
-/

@[expose] public section

